From 2026-06-13
Subject: Removed equality_saturation::simplify() from emit_expr

== Why removed ==

The simplify() call caused exponential blowup on deeply nested || chains
(32+ terms). Each Or level multiplied calls by ~6 (simplify fixpoint ×
simplify_pass recursive descent), producing 13M+ calls in 15 seconds
for a 32-term expression like word == "a" || word == "b" || ... .

See BUGS.md (2026-06-13 entry) for root cause analysis.

== Impact ==

- LLVM -O3 handles all redundant ops (add i64 0, %x → %x) that simplify
  was catching. No measurable performance regression on 7 runtime benchmarks.
- Without simplify, emit_expr no longer does peephole constant folding
  on the Briev AST before codegen. This means slightly more verbose IR,
  but the final binary is identical after LLVM optimization.

== Current state (emit_expr.rs:9) ==

    let expr = expr.clone();

== Removed code ==

    let expr = if self.optimize_budget > 0 {
        crate::analysis::equality_saturation::simplify(expr)
    } else {
        expr.clone()
    };

== How to restore ==

Apply this patch in reverse:
    git apply -R patches/2026-06-13-remove-simplify-from-emit-expr.patch

Or edit src/backend/llvm/emit_expr.rs line 9, replace:
    let expr = expr.clone();
with:
    let expr = if self.optimize_budget > 0 {
        crate::analysis::equality_saturation::simplify(expr)
    } else {
        expr.clone()
    };

== Before restoring, fix the exponential blowup ==

The simplify() function in src/analysis/equality_saturation.rs needs
a depth limit or the fixpoint loop removed before it can be safely
called from emit_expr. Current exponential structure:

    simplify(expr):
        current = simplify_pass(expr)
        for _ in 0..5:               # fixpoint
            next = simplify_pass(current)
            if same: break
            current = next

    simplify_pass(Or(l, r)):
        Or(Box::new(simplify(l)), Box::new(simplify(r)))  # ← O(6^n)

Without a depth cap, this creates O(6^n) calls for n-deep Or trees.

Possible fixes:
a) Add depth limit to simplify() — bail at depth > 10
b) Move simplify to a separate pre-codegen pass (runs once, not per node)
c) Only call simplify when has_candidates(expr) is true (avoids the
    expense for expressions with no foldable patterns)
